---
// source: 497baf7f9449
import { LEGAL_INTEREST } from '../../engine/law/data/legal-interest';
import { NORMS } from '../../engine/rental/data/norms';
import { depositReturnExample, rentalPagesCopy } from '../../content/rental-pages';
import { formatDay, formatEuros, formatRate } from '../../content/rent-indices';
import { link, type Lang } from '../../i18n/languages';

interface Props {
  lang: Lang;
}
const { lang } = Astro.props;
const { review: REVIEW, pages: RENTAL_PAGES, pageDecree } = rentalPagesCopy(lang);

const ex = depositReturnExample();
const href = (path: string) => link(lang, path.replace(/^\//, ''));
const [first, second] = ex.stretches;
if (!first || !second) throw new Error('The example spans a year change.');
const table = LEGAL_INTEREST[0]?.url;
---

<section class="sheet sheet--text" aria-labelledby="plazo">
  <h2 id="plazo">The time limit: one month from when you hand over the keys</h2>
  <p>
    When the agreement ends and you hand over the keys, the landlord has one month to return the
    deposit to you. After that month, whatever remains to be returned accrues statutory interest
    (interés legal del dinero) (art. 36.4 LAU).
  </p>
  <p>
    The month is counted from date to date: if you hand over the keys on 15 November, the time limit
    ends on 15 December and interest runs from the 16th. It runs until the day the money is returned
    to you, which no longer counts.
  </p>
  <p>
    How much deposit you can be asked for at the start:{' '}
    <a href={href(RENTAL_PAGES.deposit.path)}>{RENTAL_PAGES.deposit.name}</a>.
  </p>
  <p class="folio">
    Art. <span>36.4</span> LAU
  </p>
</section>

<section class="sheet sheet--text" aria-labelledby="interes">
  <h2 id="interes">Which interest applies</h2>
  <p>
    Statutory interest (interés legal del dinero). It is set each year by the Ley de Presupuestos
    Generales del Estado (State Budget Act), and the calculation uses the rate of the calendar year
    of each day. The rates for each year are in the <a href={table}>Banco de España's table</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The year can be counted by its calendar days (365, or 366 in a leap year) or as 360 days: we
    give both calculations.
  </p>
  <p class="folio">
    Art. <span>36.4</span> LAU
  </p>
</section>

<section class="sheet sheet--text" aria-labelledby="ejemplo">
  <h2 id="ejemplo">Worked example</h2>
  <p>
    A person with a deposit of {formatEuros(ex.deposit)} hands over the keys on{' '}
    {formatDay(ex.keysReturnedOn)}. The landlord accepts them and returns the whole deposit on{' '}
    {formatDay(ex.returnedOn)}. The month ended on 15-12-2022, so interest runs from{' '}
    {formatDay(ex.interestFrom)} and crosses the change of year, with each year's rate:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      From {formatDay(first.from)} to {formatDay(first.to)} ({first.days} days) at{' '}
      {formatRate(first.rate)}: {formatEuros(first.interest)}.
    </li>
    <li>
      From {formatDay(second.from)} to {formatDay(second.to)} ({second.days} days) at{' '}
      {formatRate(second.rate)}: {formatEuros(second.interest)}.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class="example">
    <span class="example__label">The figures</span> Each stretch is the deposit times the rate and
    times the days, divided by 100 and by the {first.yearDays} days of the year:{' '}
    {formatEuros(ex.deposit)} × {formatRate(first.rate)} × {first.days} ÷ {first.yearDays} and{' '}
    {formatEuros(ex.deposit)} × {formatRate(second.rate)} × {second.days} ÷ {second.yearDays}. In
    total, {formatEuros(ex.total)} of interest; if the year is counted as 360 days,{' '}
    {formatEuros(ex.totalCommercial)}.
  </p>
  <p class="folio">
    Art. <span>36.4</span> LAU
  </p>
</section>

<section class="sheet sheet--text" aria-labelledby="no-valoramos">
  <h2 id="no-valoramos">What we do not assess</h2>
  <p>
    If the landlord keeps part of the deposit for damage, cleaning or other items, the review notes
    each deduction as it was given to you and subtracts it from what remains to be returned. It does
    not assess whether it is justified or how much a repair costs.
  </p>
  <p>{pageDecree('deposit_return', 'rental.guide.return.closing')}</p>
  <p class="folio">
    Art. <span>36.7</span> LAU · RDL 29/2026
  </p>
</section>

<section class="sheet sheet--text" aria-labelledby="revision">
  <h2 id="revision">Calculate what remains to be returned</h2>
  <p>
    In the <a href={href(REVIEW.path)}>rental review</a> you enter when you handed over the keys,
    how much has been returned to you and when. It gives you what remains of the deposit and the
    interest, with both ways of counting the year, and can prepare a letter to request it.
  </p>
  <p>
    {NORMS.lau.citation}: <a href={NORMS.lau.url}>consolidated text in the BOE</a>.
  </p>
</section>
